# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# The Rust API reference is generated by `cargo doc` and copied into the Pages
# artifact during the deploy (issue #479); never commit the generated output.
rust/src/web/docs/api/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# See https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
# Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# IDE and editor files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python virtual environments (for scripts)
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Coverage reports. The measured numbers are regenerated on every run, but the
# reviewed baseline and the unmeasured-file inventory are the ratchet itself
# (issue #895) and must be committed so a decrease shows up in a diff.
*.lcov
lcov.info
coverage/*
!coverage/baseline.json
!coverage/browser-unmeasured.txt
tarpaulin-report.html

# Benchmark results
criterion/

# Documentation build output
doc/

# Local development files
.env
.env.local
*.local
node_modules/

# Log files
*.log
logs/
ci-logs/

# Session-log exports must never pollute a checkout root (#945, R838-1);
# the report flow writes them outside the CWD, this is defense in depth.
/formal-ai-harness-*.lino
/formal-ai-server-*.lino
!docs/case-studies/**/formal-ai-harness-*.lino
!docs/case-studies/**/formal-ai-server-*.lino

# Real Agent CLI ↔ formal-ai E2E capture, committed as case-study evidence
# (see CONTRIBUTING.md rule 8 — "Real logs in the case study, not synthesized").
!docs/case-studies/**/*.log
# ...and the directories that hold them. Git never descends into an excluded
# directory, so the rule above cannot rescue a file under one: without these,
# `git add docs/case-studies/<issue>/logs/` reports success while committing
# nothing, and the analysis ships citing evidence no reviewer can open. Issue
# #1021 lost a CI run to exactly that; `!dev/log/**/ci-logs/` is the same fix
# for the same trap one directory over.
!docs/case-studies/**/logs/
!docs/case-studies/**/ci-logs/

# Development-log CI evidence used to be committed under dev/log/ alongside
# the analysis that cited it (see dev/log/issues/*/pulls/*/ci-logs/README.md).
# Issue #1088 moves that evidence to link-assistant/formal-ai-evidence: the
# files already tracked stay tracked (git never ignores a tracked file, so
# this line is the ratchet, not the move), but nothing new may grow here.
# scripts/check-evidence-lines.rs fails a pull request that tries, and the
# sha256/size/URL record for every artifact group now lives in
# docs/evidence/index.lino.
/dev/log/

# Playwright MCP scratch output (browser cache snapshots, etc.)
.playwright-mcp/

# Per-task ref snapshot the issue #847 coding ladder writes while it runs.
experiments/issue_847_coding_ladder/.branches-before

# Web demo seed mirror (generated by scripts/sync-seed.sh from data/seed/)
# The canonical source of truth is data/seed/; the web copy is rebuilt at
# CI / dev-server start time so the browser worker can fetch the same files.
rust/src/web/seed/

# The workspace self-AST index is a deterministic aggregate of every module.
# Render it on demand with `cargo run --example dump_self_ast_census`; tracking
# it makes unrelated source branches conflict on the same generated file.
/data/meta/self-ast/index.lino

# Electron desktop packaging output generated by npm run desktop:build.
desktop/bin/
desktop/browser-runtime/
vscode/browser-runtime/
desktop/dist-web/
desktop/release/

# Semantic-identity HTTP cache populated by FORMAL_AI_LIVE_API=1. These
# directories are a local accelerator only; the committed source of
# truth for offline tests is the raw-API-response seed bundle under
# data/seed/api-cache/*.lino, bundled by rust/examples/refresh_translation_cache.rs.
data/wikidata-cache/
data/wiktionary-cache/
data/http-cache/
data/source-cache/

# The same runtime accelerators, as written by `cargo test` and the binaries
# when the working directory is the crate root `rust/` (issue #1138): the
# default cache base is the CWD-relative `data`, which now resolves one level
# down from the repository root.
rust/data/

# Per-service accessibility record (issue #991). Like the capture cache above it
# is a runtime accelerator with a 7-day TTL, rebuilt by any run that probes a
# service; the committed evidence is the QA capture manifest, not this file.
data/service-accessibility.lino
.green-ledger/
2026-*-httpsgithubcom*.txt

# Issue #953: minified web bundles are build output, not source. They are
# regenerated by `bun run build:web` (mirroring the seed-sync pattern: the
# release workflow must build before artifact upload). Sources under js/
# stay tracked; only the emitted IIFEs are ignored.
js/app.js
js/vendor.bundle.js
js/ocr.bundle.js
js/web-search-component.bundle.js

# Per-answer derivation records written by the engine at run time (issue #1184).
data/cache/derivations/
rust/data/cache/derivations/
